==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|testūdō||tortoise, turtle, lyre, type of military shelter}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|testudoes|testudines}}

# {{lb|en|Ancient Rome|military|historical}} A [[shelter#Noun|shelter]] [[form#Verb|formed]] by a [[body]] of [[troop#Noun|troops]] [[hold#Verb|holding]] their [[shield#Noun|shields]] or [[target#Noun|targets]] [[close#Adjective|close]] [[together]] over their [[head#Noun|heads]].
#: {{synonyms|en|sheltron}}
# A shelter of similar [[shape#Noun|shape]] for [[miner]]s, etc.
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} The [[fornix]].
# {{lb|en|music}} A [[kind#Noun|kind]] of [[lyre]]; so called in [[allusion]] to the lyre of [[Mercury]], [[fable#Verb|fabled]] to have been [[make#Verb|made]] of the [[shell#Noun|shell]] of a [[tortoise]].
# {{lb|en|pathology}} An [[encysted]] [[tumour]].

